The current width of the canal,
which has already been widened once,

00:29:22.560 --> 00:29:26.560
is the minimum width
for us to be able to work there.

00:29:26.960 --> 00:29:30.240
Two-way traffic is impossible

00:29:30.720 --> 00:29:33.600
when the ice is that thick.

00:29:33.920 --> 00:29:36.560
The LNG tanker
has to go first.

00:29:36.960 --> 00:29:40.000
But we cannot maneuver freely

00:29:40.640 --> 00:29:43.120
to go to the tanker's aid.

00:29:43.280 --> 00:29:46.160
There's no room for maneuver
with a 280-meter long boat,

00:29:46.400 --> 00:29:47.920
that much is clear.

00:29:49.360 --> 00:29:54.240
The director of the
Murmansk shipyard declared

00:29:54.560 --> 00:29:59.680
that the President has set a goal
of 800 commercial trips per year

00:30:00.160 --> 00:30:02.640
for the Arctic fleet.

00:30:03.200 --> 00:30:07.280
Can you imagine that?
800 trips in 365 days.

00:30:07.840 --> 00:30:10.080
It will be non-stop.

00:30:24.400 --> 00:30:28.720
In Seyakha, they shut down
the State Farm due to the constant fog

00:30:29.120 --> 00:30:31.600
and passage of the icebreakers.

00:30:31.840 --> 00:30:35.680
And when the tankers use
the Northem Sea Route,

00:30:36.160 --> 00:30:39.200
they ballast with sea water,

00:30:40.720 --> 00:30:45.200
then unballast here,
in the Ob estuary,

00:30:45.440 --> 00:30:49.920
to load the hydrocarbons.

00:30:50.400 --> 00:30:54.080
The composition of the water
has changed completely.

00:30:54.240 --> 00:30:57.200
Last year,
in the village of Seyakha,

00:30:57.360 --> 00:30:59.840
tap water turned salty.

00:31:19.840 --> 00:31:23.520
There used to be 97 brigades
of reindeer herders.

00:31:24.480 --> 00:31:27.600
Today, there's only
half that number.

00:31:30.240 --> 00:31:35.840
We estimate that 60 to 70%
of the indigenous population

00:31:36.240 --> 00:31:39.440
live under the poverty line,

00:31:39.840 --> 00:31:42.720
even though the region
is so rich.

00:31:43.280 --> 00:31:45.680
It's not normal.

00:32:32.360 --> 00:32:45.480
Their way of dealing with the advancement of the gas industry is not taking a total opposition and saying we are going to defend our land against the gas industry because it can only happen in conflict.

00:32:46.440 --> 00:32:53.960
They try to find ways in which they can continue their own lifestyle in spite of having the gas industry on their land.

00:32:57.800 --> 00:33:01.160
And if Moscow says that that deposit is going to be developed,

00:33:01.920 --> 00:33:03.080
these people are not stupid.

00:33:03.120 --> 00:33:04.680
They know that if Moscow says it,

00:33:04.680 --> 00:33:05.520
it will be developed,

00:33:05.560 --> 00:33:06.000
full stop.

00:33:12.160 --> 00:33:13.760
This industry is too big a thing.

00:33:13.840 --> 00:33:16.080
The Nenets wouldn't be able to resist it completely.

00:33:16.440 --> 00:33:17.880
They wouldn't be able to veto it,

00:33:18.040 --> 00:33:19.840
because they don't have the rights to do that.

00:33:25.600 --> 00:33:26.600
There's no way they can say,

00:33:26.640 --> 00:33:26.800
oh,

00:33:26.800 --> 00:33:29.720
we don't want the Bovinenkova deposit to be extracted.

00:33:30.280 --> 00:33:32.560
They can have something to say about smaller issues,

00:33:33.040 --> 00:33:40.480
and I think this dedication to the smaller issues is what rescued a lot of the lifestyle that we can still see today.

00:34:14.880 --> 00:34:18.400
The reindeer and the Nenets
are as one.

00:34:19.600 --> 00:34:22.720
It's innate.

00:34:26.160 --> 00:34:29.520
We live in symbiosis
with nature.

00:34:34.160 --> 00:34:37.840
In the e tundra,
there's no such thing as bad weather.

00:34:38.240 --> 00:34:42.320
We work in all weather,
and in unison with the weather.

00:34:43.360 --> 00:34:45.680
Nature is freedom.

00:34:48.960 --> 00:34:51.440
Vika, your little brother's crying!

00:34:52.400 --> 00:34:54.160
Come on, hurry up!

00:34:55.760 --> 00:35:00.240
A swift girl, an agile girl..

00:35:06.000 --> 00:35:07.360
Kolya, come here.

00:35:07.760 --> 00:35:09.280
He's found something.

00:35:14.320 --> 00:35:16.800
Shall I sew it from outside
or inside?

00:35:17.120 --> 00:35:19.520
Won't you wear another coat?
- No.

00:35:19.680 --> 00:35:22.880
So take it off
and tell me where it's torn.

00:35:23.120 --> 00:35:25.840
The side of the mitten,
on the right.

00:35:31.120 --> 00:35:36.000
In the tundra,
a man without a wife,

00:35:37.040 --> 00:35:39.600
is no longer a man.

00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:42.320
He cannot live without her.

00:35:42.880 --> 00:35:45.280
But a woman
without a man,

00:35:45.440 --> 00:35:47.200
say for example he dies,

00:35:47.360 --> 00:35:50.320
will survive easily.
She knows how to do everything.

00:35:51.040 --> 00:35:52.640
She cares for the reindeer.

00:35:52.800 --> 00:35:54.960
She ensures there's heating,
cares for the children.

00:35:55.120 --> 00:35:58.000
She can mount a tent
and migrate alone.

00:35:58.240 --> 00:36:03.840
The most important thing
is to have support:

00:36:04.720 --> 00:36:09.040
a brigade, or neighbors
who can  guide her.

00:36:09.200 --> 00:36:10.960
She can follow them.

00:36:11.360 --> 00:36:14.160
Yes, she can do everything.

00:36:14.720 --> 00:36:17.120
But a man cannot live
without a woman.

00:36:17.280 --> 00:36:19.040
He disappears immediately.

00:36:33.520 --> 00:36:37.360
The gas flares burn,
the climate changes.

00:36:37.600 --> 00:36:41.280
The extraction of gas
leads to a change in temperature.

00:36:43.120 --> 00:36:45.040
Sometimes it's cold,

00:36:45.280 --> 00:36:48.240
sometimes spring comes early,
sometimes too late.

00:36:48.480 --> 00:36:50.800
Sometimes winter is milder.

00:36:51.600 --> 00:36:56.000
All that is because
of gas extraction.

00:37:02.080 --> 00:37:04.720
It didn't use to be like this.

00:37:05.680 --> 00:37:07.440
Nature was intact.

00:37:07.840 --> 00:37:10.560
They are destroying nature.

00:37:11.120 --> 00:37:13.040
Where they are operating,

00:37:13.280 --> 00:37:16.320
there are gas flares
and emissions.

00:37:16.480 --> 00:37:20.080
It's impossible to live
near Bovanenkovo

00:37:20.800 --> 00:37:29.120
Within a 25 km radius
there are smoke emissions

00:37:31.280 --> 00:37:34.960
and ashes from flares.

00:37:35.600 --> 00:37:39.440
The ashes fly around
and land on the ground.

00:37:39.600 --> 00:37:47.840
There is no pasture land
within a 25 km radius.

00:37:48.880 --> 00:37:52.880
Naturally,
Bovanenkovo is vast.

00:37:56.080 --> 00:38:00.160
I have been there several times.

00:38:00.960 --> 00:38:04.160
These days,
it's warmer there than here.

00:38:04.720 --> 00:38:07.520
The geese arrive there earlier
than they do here

00:38:07.760 --> 00:38:11.840
They follow a warm current,
the Gulf Stream.

00:38:12.240 --> 00:38:15.520
When we get there
the geese have already arrived.

00:38:16.000 --> 00:38:18.640
I don't know
what the future holds for us.

00:38:20.480 --> 00:38:23.120
I don't have
the slightest idea.

00:38:45.600 --> 00:38:51.560
Most of the hydrocarbons that are in the Arctic are located on the Russian side and those will be developed.

00:38:51.760 --> 00:39:06.920
That's what's driving our current climate problem and so it's kind of ironic that obviously as the Arctic opens up and you can now start drilling and extracting more resources such as oil and gas and that's just going to further amplify the climate change that we're going through.

00:39:21.120 --> 00:39:26.160
There is a lot of methane
in this region.

00:39:31.680 --> 00:39:33.600
When it rains,

00:39:33.840 --> 00:39:37.200
the water starts
to accumulate.

00:39:39.520 --> 00:39:43.520
When the reindeer stamp on the ground,
it starts to move.

00:39:47.280 --> 00:39:52.400
There is 50 cm of mud,
then sand,

00:39:52.640 --> 00:39:54.800
and below that
is the permafrost.

00:40:06.160 --> 00:40:09.640
You're warming the Arctic up so much faster and all the permafrost areas are thawing.

00:40:10.160 --> 00:40:14.600
And that's going to affect all the plant species as well as the animal species in the Arctic as well.

00:40:15.760 --> 00:40:16.920
The ice is melting faster,

00:40:17.040 --> 00:40:18.480
the permafrost is thawing faster.

00:40:18.480 --> 00:40:18.640
I mean,

00:40:18.680 --> 00:40:20.280
all of these are interconnected.

00:40:26.640 --> 00:40:30.840
It's just that there are traditional indicators of how they understand the climate system,

00:40:31.240 --> 00:40:36.320
how they understand storms and ice conditions and species migration.

00:40:36.520 --> 00:40:38.680
All of that is changing as a result of climate change,

00:40:38.720 --> 00:40:43.640
because I think the pace that we're seeing today in the changes that are happening in the Arctic is so fast,

00:40:44.040 --> 00:40:46.680
much faster than anything that's happened in the historical past.

00:40:48.800 --> 00:40:53.280
So that's why their traditional ways of knowledge aren't working anymore.

00:41:53.760 --> 00:41:58.240
The water used to go up
to the banks.

00:41:59.040 --> 00:42:03.520
Now it has lowered
and the banks are visible.

00:42:04.880 --> 00:42:08.720
It's now difficult to climb
with a loaded sled.

00:42:09.840 --> 00:42:12.240
Many tip over.

00:42:13.280 --> 00:42:16.240
Here, the current
is always the same.

00:42:16.720 --> 00:42:19.840
When we head for the Kara Sea,
it's much stronger.

00:42:20.000 --> 00:42:23.120
On this side of the river,

00:42:23.360 --> 00:42:26.640
there is a lot of erosion
when it rains.

00:42:27.920 --> 00:42:30.800
It's sandy and soft.

00:42:31.840 --> 00:42:35.200
When it rains,
it erodes easily.

00:42:36.240 --> 00:42:40.640
Sometimes,
we have to dig with spades

00:42:42.000 --> 00:42:45.440
to allow the sled
to get up or down.

00:42:45.760 --> 00:42:49.760
The descent must be feasible
and the climb doable.

00:43:06.040 --> 00:43:14.280
He committed suicide after an oil and gas consultation with the company Amoco back in the

00:43:14.280 --> 00:43:15.440
1990s.

00:43:19.800 --> 00:43:20.440
After this,

00:43:21.400 --> 00:43:31.360
he thought that that would be the end of the life for that group of reindeer nomads.

00:43:32.360 --> 00:43:33.360
And he couldn't stand that.

00:43:37.960 --> 00:43:38.440
It's really,

00:43:38.480 --> 00:43:45.920
really nice also for his legacy to see that his son and his grandchildren are still moving on the same land.

00:44:09.920 --> 00:44:12.480
It's the most complicated stretch.

00:44:26.320 --> 00:44:31.440
Each brigade has
its own route and pastures.

00:44:31.840 --> 00:44:35.040
We do not want
to disturb each other.

00:44:41.920 --> 00:44:45.360
The constant sound of the gas flares

00:44:46.000 --> 00:44:51.120
can even wake a heavy sleeper.

00:44:52.800 --> 00:44:57.040
We have no choice,
we have to get used to it.

00:44:58.960 --> 00:45:00.880
It's impossible to get to sleep,

00:45:01.200 --> 00:45:04.800
but those who sleep deeply
feel like they're sleeping.

00:45:52.880 --> 00:45:56.400
The winter of 2013-2014
was normal.

00:46:00.800 --> 00:46:06.720
Then, suddenly, there was a thaw,
with fog and rain.

00:46:07.200 --> 00:46:10.400
The snow started to melt.

00:46:11.360 --> 00:46:17.920
The temperature rose to 5°C.

00:46:20.640 --> 00:46:24.880
Then snowstorms came
from the north.

00:46:25.440 --> 00:46:28.720
The temperature dropped
down to -25°C.

00:46:32.560 --> 00:46:35.120
The reindeer couldn't reach
the lichen to feed.

00:46:36.000 --> 00:46:40.480
There was packed snow
to that depth.

00:46:42.160 --> 00:46:46.560
And half of that crust was ice.

00:47:01.600 --> 00:47:05.520
The wind from the north
was very cold.

00:47:06.480 --> 00:47:10.480
Nocturnal temperatures
dropped to -30°C.

00:47:10.800 --> 00:47:14.160
During the day,
it rose to -25°C.

00:47:15.040 --> 00:47:17.600
It was mid-April.

00:47:19.520 --> 00:47:22.160
The reindeer started to disperse.

00:47:23.440 --> 00:47:26.400
We hung on for the first
two or three days,

00:47:27.120 --> 00:47:32.000
but on the fourth day,
the reindeer scattered.

00:47:33.520 --> 00:47:38.000
Thanks to the work
of my sons Alik and Roman,

00:47:38.160 --> 00:47:40.880
we brought them back together.

00:47:41.520 --> 00:47:45.200
We managed to move them

00:47:46.640 --> 00:47:53.120
to pastures
where there was more lichen.

00:47:54.160 --> 00:47:57.600
That's how we held out
during that difficult time.

00:47:59.920 --> 00:48:05.360
Some nights,
we barely slept.

00:48:09.280 --> 00:48:12.320
We lost around 200 reindeer.

00:48:16.160 --> 00:48:22.720
Some perished,
others escaped.

00:48:25.760 --> 00:48:34.720
Without the help of our friends
living in the city,

00:48:37.440 --> 00:48:39.680
we wouldn't have survived.

00:48:41.600 --> 00:48:48.320
Several herds disappeared
and died of hunger.

00:48:54.240 --> 00:48:57.520
There are times
when all you do is survive.

00:48:57.760 --> 00:49:00.240
Yes, you have to hang in there.

00:49:14.600 --> 00:49:14.720
In

00:49:14.720 --> 00:49:16.480
the winter of 2014,

00:49:17.520 --> 00:49:20.720
more than a quarter of the reindeer died in the Yamal Peninsula.

00:49:49.680 --> 00:49:55.360
We're trying to regulate
the price of meat, which is too low.

00:49:56.080 --> 00:50:02.160
I go round the administrations
to defend our budget.

00:50:05.440 --> 00:50:07.120
On our migratory routes,

00:50:07.280 --> 00:50:11.040
there are gas drilling stations
every 50-60 km.

00:50:11.200 --> 00:50:14.880
Where can
the reindeer herders go?

00:50:15.440 --> 00:50:19.280
They must go elsewhere.
We have money.

00:50:19.760 --> 00:50:21.920
With this money,

00:50:22.080 --> 00:50:28.480
we can set up programs
to support the herders.

00:50:29.120 --> 00:50:33.040
Reindeer herding is
first and foremost a way of life,

00:50:33.200 --> 00:50:36.080
it is a set of traditions,
a culture.

00:50:36.240 --> 00:50:39.520
They supply meat
to the State,

00:50:39.760 --> 00:50:43.600
which supports them
by buying it at 450 rubles the kilo,

00:50:44.080 --> 00:50:46.080
a very good price.

00:50:46.240 --> 00:50:48.320
The price in the shops
is lower

00:50:48.480 --> 00:50:51.040
than what the State
pays the herders.

00:50:51.280 --> 00:50:53.040
All summer
he gave me to believe

00:50:53.200 --> 00:50:55.520
that the price of meat
would go up to 450 rubles,

00:50:55.680 --> 00:50:58.240
and he encouraged me
to slaughter reindeer.

00:50:58.800 --> 00:51:02.880
"What are you doing?
You're tricking people."

00:51:04.400 --> 00:51:08.800
For five years, we have been
negotiating a rise in the price of meat

00:51:09.040 --> 00:51:12.000
so that the herders
can make a decent living.

00:51:12.240 --> 00:51:16.240
A document announces
that meat will soon cost 450 rubles.

00:51:16.400 --> 00:51:20.560
But they will not buy it
at that price.

00:51:21.360 --> 00:51:25.520
They say: "Herders,
slaughter your reindeer!"

00:51:26.160 --> 00:51:31.600
They're doing it
to reduce the reindeer population.

00:51:32.560 --> 00:51:34.400
They say they'll raise the price,

00:51:34.560 --> 00:51:37.680
hoping it will incite herders
to slaughter more.

00:51:53.360 --> 00:51:56.720
The villages get bigger,
which is probably good.

00:51:56.880 --> 00:51:58.720
Yar-Sale is growing.

00:52:00.160 --> 00:52:05.200
Gazprom's presence
spurs construction.

00:52:05.760 --> 00:52:09.440
But for the reindeer herders,

00:52:11.280 --> 00:52:13.920
there is nothing of interest.

00:52:15.440 --> 00:52:19.040
It's a good thing
for children to be able to study.

00:52:19.680 --> 00:52:24.080
Boarding schools are built
and Gazprom finances everything.

00:52:26.800 --> 00:52:33.120
The boarding school system
came into being a long time ago.

00:52:33.920 --> 00:52:38.480
Our grandparents already went
to boarding school.

00:52:38.800 --> 00:52:42.320
It's part of our life now.

00:52:44.080 --> 00:52:48.160
Even the last child
in the family

00:52:51.280 --> 00:52:54.640
is sent to boarding school.

00:52:55.120 --> 00:52:58.720
They can get an education.

00:52:58.720 --> 00:52:58.960
adidas adidas
They can get an education.

00:53:00.160 --> 00:53:02.640
It's essential.

00:53:12.000 --> 00:53:16.480
Modern reindeer herders
need to be educated.

00:53:19.600 --> 00:53:22.720
They have to understand.

00:53:24.720 --> 00:53:30.240
The reindeer will not disappear
in the 21st century.

00:53:30.640 --> 00:53:32.560
Some of my grandchildren

00:53:33.520 --> 00:53:37.440
will stay in the tundra
and raise reindeer.

00:53:53.280 --> 00:53:59.200
Strength, endurance, speed,
I have all you need to be a herder.

00:54:03.760 --> 00:54:08.080
I can catch reindeer,
I can fish.

00:54:09.040 --> 00:54:10.880
I know how to survive.

00:54:11.040 --> 00:54:16.640
If reindeer wander off,
you have to go and get them.

00:54:16.960 --> 00:54:22.080
You have to be able
to find your way back.

00:54:27.680 --> 00:54:31.200
One foggy day,
I got lost.

00:54:32.000 --> 00:54:35.920
I was alone, I couldn't see
the camp and it was raining.

00:54:39.680 --> 00:54:44.160
Another time,
I was looking after the herd on my own.

00:54:44.720 --> 00:54:49.120
I did 30 km on a sled,
in the snow.

00:54:53.920 --> 00:54:59.200
It took around 15 hours.

00:54:59.840 --> 00:55:01.680
It worked out.

00:55:05.920 --> 00:55:08.640
I used the moon and stars
to navigate,

00:55:09.040 --> 00:55:12.640
and there were places
that I recognized.

00:55:21.120 --> 00:55:25.840
I love to throw the lasso
to catch reindeer.

00:55:27.440 --> 00:55:29.520
And then there's hunting.

00:55:34.720 --> 00:55:38.160
It's impossible to put
these emotions into words.

00:55:45.120 --> 00:55:49.360
I will stay here.
I want to migrate.

00:55:50.320 --> 00:55:52.720
I want to live a nomadic life.

00:56:12.960 --> 00:56:16.800
The tundra is everything to me.

00:56:18.240 --> 00:56:22.880
Here, it's not like in the city.
There is freedom.

00:56:24.400 --> 00:56:29.840
There is no noise,
no cars, no asphalt.

00:56:30.720 --> 00:56:33.920
To live in town
or in the tundra?

00:56:34.960 --> 00:56:42.560
That will be my decision
and mine alone.

00:56:50.640 --> 00:56:54.640
But I would like
to live in town and work.

00:56:55.680 --> 00:56:58.960
I would be able to help my family,

00:56:59.840 --> 00:57:04.160
my nephews, my nieces
and my brothers.

00:57:05.120 --> 00:57:07.120
I want to make their lives easier.

00:57:07.280 --> 00:57:11.360
When I'm at boarding school,
the hardest thing

00:57:11.680 --> 00:57:16.080
is waiting nine months
to see my parents.

00:57:16.400 --> 00:57:19.760
And then to see them
only for a few days.

00:57:20.720 --> 00:57:24.080
That's why I want
to stay in town.

00:57:25.360 --> 00:57:28.640
If I lived in the tundra,

00:57:28.800 --> 00:57:31.680
I would I be worried
for my future children.

00:57:32.240 --> 00:57:36.640
How long would I have to wait
before I could see them?

00:57:37.040 --> 00:57:39.280
It would be very complicated.

00:57:41.560 --> 00:57:42.280
In the tundra,

00:57:42.680 --> 00:57:44.360
children leave the camp for nine months.

00:57:46.880 --> 00:57:48.960
This is the last summer morning.

00:57:59.600 --> 00:58:02.480
Eynye, are you going
to wash your face?

00:58:04.320 --> 00:58:05.440
Yes!

00:58:06.000 --> 00:58:08.880
Vika, your little brother.
Take him!

00:58:10.320 --> 00:58:12.800
Vika!
Tolik, take him!

00:58:12.960 --> 00:58:14.000
Tolik!

00:58:14.880 --> 00:58:16.800
Don't move.

00:58:18.880 --> 00:58:22.240
Stop it, you're cold.

00:58:23.760 --> 00:58:27.840
That's what I'm saying,
you have some coffee too.

00:58:28.160 --> 00:58:30.160
We're not having any.

00:58:30.400 --> 00:58:32.320
You're out of coffee!

00:58:32.720 --> 00:58:36.080
Get dressed quickly,
I'll give it to you outside.

00:59:16.480 --> 00:59:17.920
Vika, stand there.

00:59:18.320 --> 00:59:20.320
Hurry, Vika,
the chopper's about to leave.

00:59:22.960 --> 00:59:24.480
Kolya, look over here.

00:59:26.960 --> 00:59:28.560
It's not the right chopper!

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:33.120
It's very hard.

01:01:34.000 --> 01:01:36.720
Lots of people live together
in the tent,

01:01:36.960 --> 01:01:40.720
and suddenly
our parents are all alone.

01:01:43.920 --> 01:01:47.200
It's sad.
It's too quiet.

01:01:47.680 --> 01:01:50.960
No more kids,
running all over the place.

01:02:02.480 --> 01:02:08.000
And we think we'll wake up
in the tent with our family -

01:02:08.880 --> 01:02:12.480
then we remember
that we're in town.

01:02:13.360 --> 01:02:17.440
Stuck between four walls,

01:02:18.480 --> 01:02:21.840
and our loved ones
are no longer there.

01:02:32.560 --> 01:02:37.200
You tell yourself
that when you leave the tundra,

01:02:37.440 --> 01:02:40.160
all will be well.

01:02:40.560 --> 01:02:43.360
But you cry anyway.

01:02:44.720 --> 01:02:47.360
It's impossible
not to be sad.

01:02:47.760 --> 01:02:49.920
I realize

01:02:50.080 --> 01:02:53.040
that I'll only see them again
in winter,

01:02:53.360 --> 01:02:56.000
in many months' time.

01:03:18.000 --> 01:03:19.120
11A

01:03:19.440 --> 01:03:21.120
As always,

01:03:21.280 --> 01:03:24.800
on September 1st
our family welcomes its new pupils.

01:03:24.960 --> 01:03:28.160
Today, we have
202 new pupils.

01:03:31.120 --> 01:03:35.120
Dear new pupils,
I wish you success.

01:03:42.160 --> 01:03:43.840
Those who come from the tundra,

01:03:44.000 --> 01:03:46.640
who have lived with their family,
in small communities,

01:03:47.040 --> 01:03:49.680
find it a little hard at first,

01:03:49.840 --> 01:03:52.800
because we have
over 1,500 children.

01:03:54.240 --> 01:03:57.840
All of a sudden,
they're part of a big community,

01:03:58.640 --> 01:04:01.360
and they have
to find their place.

01:04:39.040 --> 01:04:40.720
It's always like that.

01:04:41.520 --> 01:04:43.440
Is it Ilyushka?
- Yes.

01:04:47.040 --> 01:04:49.440
Did you add bread to the meatballs?
- Yes.

01:04:59.920 --> 01:05:02.400
Tolik's doing a back flip
in slow motion.

01:05:19.200 --> 01:05:20.720
I took my phone too.

01:05:20.880 --> 01:05:23.040
We said many goodbyes
to Théodore when he left.

01:05:23.200 --> 01:05:24.800
He cried.

01:05:28.720 --> 01:05:31.120
It's the first day
that the foreigners arrived.

01:05:31.840 --> 01:05:34.960
Time flew by too fast.
- As always.

01:05:35.200 --> 01:05:36.640
He did it on his own.

01:05:41.360 --> 01:05:43.440
Tolik does it well.

01:05:43.680 --> 01:05:46.000
What a champ!

01:05:47.680 --> 01:05:48.880
Look.

01:05:49.680 --> 01:05:51.920
What?
- Anti-stress.

01:05:53.280 --> 01:05:54.320
Nadya?

01:05:55.840 --> 01:05:58.720
Could you bring
an armful of firewood?

01:06:33.680 --> 01:06:38.000
No one forces me
to do this,

01:06:38.480 --> 01:06:42.480
but I feel
a sense of responsibility,

01:06:42.880 --> 01:06:44.960
because I live here.

01:06:45.200 --> 01:06:49.360
So I take them to my home
each weekend,

01:06:49.600 --> 01:06:54.320
to get them away
from boarding school life,

01:06:54.480 --> 01:06:57.520
to give them a home atmosphere

01:06:57.840 --> 01:07:01.760
and good home cooking,

01:07:01.920 --> 01:07:05.520
fish, meat, berries.

01:07:05.840 --> 01:07:08.160
Over the two days
of the weekend,

01:07:08.880 --> 01:07:12.080
they feel some of the comforts
of their tundra home.

01:07:12.400 --> 01:07:16.160
In winter, we snowmobile,
in summer, we pick berries.

01:07:16.400 --> 01:07:21.280
Afterwards, they can cope
with another week at school.

01:07:48.800 --> 01:07:50.560
What shall we sing?

01:07:55.040 --> 01:07:57.200
You're a bee,
I'm a beekeeper.

01:07:57.360 --> 01:07:58.960
Ah, we love honey.

01:07:59.120 --> 01:08:00.640
I'm going to be lucky.

01:08:00.800 --> 01:08:03.040
I'm going to be lucky
with you.

01:08:03.520 --> 01:08:06.160
It's important

01:08:08.720 --> 01:08:12.960
that there be changes
for the young Nenets.

01:08:13.360 --> 01:08:19.440
There are few Nenets
with university degrees.

01:08:21.520 --> 01:08:26.480
As children
of herders in the tundra,

01:08:26.960 --> 01:08:34.640
they are offered
a limited range of professions:

01:08:35.120 --> 01:08:39.920
veterinarian,
zootechnician, or teacher.

01:08:40.480 --> 01:08:45.920
Teachers and professors
who are not Nenet

01:08:46.320 --> 01:08:49.680
consider these children
of the tundra

01:08:49.920 --> 01:08:54.400
to have limited
cognitive capacities.

01:08:54.560 --> 01:08:58.880
There is no interest
in improving the quality of education

01:08:59.120 --> 01:09:04.720
to enable these young people
to go to university.

01:09:05.040 --> 01:09:08.080
It's a vicious circle.

01:09:12.960 --> 01:09:15.600
The nomadic life could disappear.

01:09:16.400 --> 01:09:21.200
Today,
it is on the brink of survival.

01:09:22.480 --> 01:09:27.600
It will either get worse,
or stagnate.

01:09:35.440 --> 01:09:43.440
50 % of the population
will probably become sedentary.

01:09:59.520 --> 01:10:04.320
What will the herders do
in the village, without reindeer?

01:10:13.280 --> 01:10:18.480
My brothers
who live in the tundra

01:10:20.000 --> 01:10:23.280
raise reindeer.

01:10:26.560 --> 01:10:33.520
Will my brothers live in tents,
near Yar-Sale?

01:10:35.280 --> 01:10:37.200
What will they do?

01:11:06.560 --> 01:11:11.600
We will extract more and more
hydrocarbons from the ocean.

01:11:11.760 --> 01:11:17.520
Should we engage in extraction
from the Arctic Shelves?

01:11:17.920 --> 01:11:22.400
The answer is obvious:
yes, we must.

01:11:23.280 --> 01:11:26.880
Gazprom is actively working on it.

01:11:26.880 --> 01:11:27.200
Y

01:11:27.440 --> 01:11:30.960
The Northern Sea Route
is actively being explored.

01:11:31.680 --> 01:11:35.360
By 2050,

01:11:37.200 --> 01:11:41.280
the Arctic Shelves
of Russia and other countries 

01:11:41.440 --> 01:11:46.080
be among the main suppliersof hydrocarbons

01:11:46.400 --> 01:11:48.400
to world markets.

01:12:00.560 --> 01:12:01.280
Like Vasili,

01:12:02.080 --> 01:12:03.760
I don't know what tomorrow will bring,

01:12:04.360 --> 01:12:08.320
facing both climate change and crazy gas extraction.

01:12:09.680 --> 01:12:12.120
The Nanats will have to rely on their strengths,

01:12:13.520 --> 01:12:14.520
their knowledge of nature,

01:12:15.720 --> 01:12:18.040
and their capacity for resilience to survive,

01:12:19.040 --> 01:12:24.640
as the backbone of which is the transhuman's route that they have walked for generations.

01:12:34.400 --> 01:12:37.280
Nature is strong,
it recovers quickly.

01:12:38.080 --> 01:12:41.840
It doesn't like damage,
it heals itself rapidly,

01:12:42.240 --> 01:12:45.120
as a body does a wound.

01:12:45.840 --> 01:12:48.000
For upcoming generations,
not much will change.

01:12:48.320 --> 01:12:50.480
But gas is not inexhaustible,
it will run out.

01:12:50.720 --> 01:12:54.400
After that, the earth will heal
and be even better than before

